<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">23 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 23 March, from 625 to 1965.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">625 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,401 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Quraysh defeat the Muslims at the Battle of Uhud</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near Mount Uhud, north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quraysh">Quraysh</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> under Abu Sufyan defeated the Muslims under Muhammad after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archery">archers</a> left their posts. Muhammad was wounded and his uncle Hamza killed, but the Meccans did not follow up their victory.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-uhud">Battle of Uhud</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad">Muhammad</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quraysh">Quraysh</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1400">1400 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">626 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hồ Quý Ly deposes the Trần dynasty and founds the Hồ dynasty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ho-quy-ly">Hồ Quý Ly</a> overthrew the emperor Thiếu Đế, his own grandson, ending 175 years of Trần rule in Đại Việt and founding the Hồ dynasty. The Ming used his usurpation as a pretext to invade in 1406.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ho-quy-ly">Hồ Quý Ly</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1540">1540 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">486 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Waltham Abbey surrenders, the last English monastery to close</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Augustinian abbey at Waltham in Essex was surrendered to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a>'s commissioners. It completed the Dissolution of the Monasteries, which transferred vast church lands to the Crown.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1775">1775 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">251 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Patrick Henry declares 'Give me liberty, or give me death!'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the Second <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a> Convention in Richmond, Henry urged the colony to raise a militia against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>. The convention agreed, and fighting began at Lexington four weeks later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/tsar" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tsar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1801">1801 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">225 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tsar Paul I murdered in St Michael's Castle</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Conspiring officers killed the erratic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> in his bedroom in St Petersburg. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-i-of-russia">Alexander I</a>, aware of the plot, succeeded him and later led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1919">1919 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">107 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mussolini founds the Fasci di Combattimento in Milan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Benito Mussolini</a> gathered veterans and nationalists in Piazza San Sepolcro to found a new movement. Its blackshirts helped him take power in 1922, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fascism">Fascism</a> became a model for Hitler.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Benito Mussolini</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fascism">Fascism</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1933">1933 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">93 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Reichstag passes the Enabling Act</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With communists barred and others intimidated, the German parliament allowed Hitler's cabinet to make laws without it. Only the Social Democrats voted against, and the dictatorship had a legal basis.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reichstag">Reichstag</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1965">1965 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">61 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gemini 3 makes the first crewed Gemini flight</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Gus Grissom and John Young flew three orbits and became the first astronauts to change their spacecraft's orbit. The Gemini programme prepared the techniques for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a>.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 23 March <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-go-kogon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-go-kogon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Emperor Go-Kōgon</span><span class="tp">1338–1374</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/margaret-of-anjou"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/margaret-of-anjou.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Margaret of Anjou</span><span class="tp">1430–1482</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/michael-joseph-savage"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/michael-joseph-savage.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Michael Joseph Savage</span><span class="tp">1872–1940</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 23 March <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-zhenzong-of-song"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Emperor Zhenzong of Song</span><span class="tp">968–1022</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/peter-of-castile"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/peter-of-castile.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Peter of Castile</span><span class="tp">1334–1369</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/yolande-duchess-of-lorraine"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/yolande-duchess-of-lorraine.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Yolande, Duchess of Lorraine</span><span class="tp">1428–1483</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/luis-donaldo-colosio"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Luis Donaldo Colosio</span><span class="tp">1950–1994</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/adolfo-suarez"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/adolfo-suarez.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Adolfo Suárez</span><span class="tp">1932–2014</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/lee-kuan-yew"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lee-kuan-yew.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Lee Kuan Yew</span><span class="tp">1923–2015</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
